comments.body:
I am down for using a cleanup method instead rather than introducing IDs and making the state manager aware of those IDS. We may need this in the future but right now I don't think this is needed.

The reasoning behind using a cleanup method like this:

```js
cleanup: function(state) {
  return omit(state, attributeName);
}
```

rather than having to specify an ID in a connector is that it's more in line with the way connectors need to handle the state today. They need to handle it fully (in refine methods)

I see IDs and automatic cleaning of IDs a bit magical and doing things in the background (in state manager) that are sometime being done in the foreground (in the connector, in refine).
